  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_006 (RNA-only, multi-profile, scVI n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc, and the RNA-only space appears well-characterized (scVI n200 >> PCA/scGPT; multi-profile >> single-profile; transformer ≈ avgpool). The key unexplored question is whether adding the image modality to this already-optimized RNA pipeline yields complementary signal or merely dilutes it, given that image-only ResNet50 scored only 0.208. Config_032 (multimodal, multi-profile, scVI n200, ResNet50, transformer, concat) is the most direct and minimal extension of config_006: it changes only the model setting from RNA-only to multimodal with the simplest fusion (concat), isolating the effect of adding image. If concat fusion helps, a follow-up with weighted fusion (config_033) could further tune the balance; if it hurts, we confirm the RNA signal is self-sufficient and can spend remaining budget on other refinements. With 3 experiments left, this single test gives the highest information gain about whether the multimodal direction is worth further investment."
}

